From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [server,proxy] drop Server Status Info PDUs the front client
 did not announce

pf_client_server_status_info() forwarded every Server Status Info PDU
([MS-RDPBCGR] 2.2.5.2) of the back-end to the front client. A client
announces support with RNS_UD_CS_SUPPORT_STATUSINFO_PDU in the
earlyCapabilityFlags of its Client Core Data (2.2.1.3.2), and 3.3.5.7.2
says that the server MUST NOT send the PDU otherwise.

On the front, FreeRDP_SupportStatusInfoPdu holds exactly that: TRUE by
default in server mode, cleared by updateEarlyClientCaps() when the
client did not set the flag. The back-end hop starts from a copy of the
front settings and advertises the same flag, so a conforming back-end
stays quiet. A back-end that sends the PDU anyway, or a back-end hop
whose settings a module changed, made the proxy break the rule towards
its client.

Check the front's setting before forwarding and drop the PDU with a
debug message when the client did not announce support. Forwarding is
unchanged otherwise.
---
 server/proxy/pf_update.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/server/proxy/pf_update.c b/server/proxy/pf_update.c
index ce88322..f49b62f 100644
--- a/server/proxy/pf_update.c
+++ b/server/proxy/pf_update.c
@@ -346,6 +346,18 @@ static BOOL pf_client_server_status_info(rdpContext* context, UINT32 status)
 	WINPR_ASSERT(ps->context.update->ServerStatusInfo);

 	WLog_DBG(TAG, "called");
+
+	/* [MS-RDPBCGR] 3.3.5.7.2: the server MUST NOT send a Server Status Info PDU
+	 * unless the client set RNS_UD_CS_SUPPORT_STATUSINFO_PDU in its Client Core Data. */
+	if (!freerdp_settings_get_bool(ps->context.settings, FreeRDP_SupportStatusInfoPdu))
+	{
+		PROXY_LOG_DBG(TAG, pc,
+		              "dropping server status info 0x%08" PRIx32
+		              ": front client did not announce RNS_UD_CS_SUPPORT_STATUSINFO_PDU",
+		              status);
+		return TRUE;
+	}
+
 	return ps->context.update->ServerStatusInfo(&ps->context, status);
 }

